# Build context for deploy/docker/*/Dockerfile. Compose builds every image with
# the repository root as context, so this file decides what reaches the Docker
# daemon or a remote builder.
#
# It is an ALLOWLIST: exclude everything, then re-include exactly the paths the
# Dockerfiles COPY. When a Dockerfile starts copying a new path, add a "!" rule
# below; the CI "containers" job builds every image, so a missing rule fails
# fast with "not found" instead of silently shipping extra files.
#
#   control-plane: server/, database/migrations/
#   worker:        server/, database/migrations/, go.mod, go.sum, backend/
#   frontend:      desktop/vue3-ui/, frontend/src/resources/images/logo.png,
#                  deploy/nginx/frontend.conf
#
# Everything else stays out, notably .git, .codex-tmp, bin/ (~350 MB of
# git-tracked xray/sing-box connector binaries), local browser profiles and
# runtime data, publish/ and build/ outputs, and deploy/.env*. Compose reads
# deploy/.env and deploy/.env.example on the client; no image copies them.
*

!server/
!database/migrations/
!go.mod
!go.sum
!backend/
!desktop/vue3-ui/
!frontend/src/resources/images/logo.png
!deploy/nginx/frontend.conf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hard excludes. Keep these AFTER the re-includes: the last matching rule wins,
# so they also apply inside re-included directories and cannot be undone by a
# "!" rule added above.

# Host dependency trees and tool caches. Images run npm ci / go mod download
# themselves, and host node_modules can contain platform-specific binaries.
**/node_modules
**/.vite
**/coverage

# Secrets and machine-local overrides, at any depth.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.local
**/*.local.json
**/*.local.yaml
**/*.local.yml

# Local runtime data, logs and build/test artifacts.
**/*.log
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.test
**/*.out
**/*.exe
**/.DS_Store

# Connector binaries, browser cores/profiles and user data must never enter a
# cloud image build context. Already excluded by "*"; listed so that no future
# re-include can pull them back in.
bin
connectors
browser-cores
browser-data
user-data
data
chrome
